# Copy to `.env.test` and point TEST_DATABASE_URL at a local PostgreSQL you are
# willing to lose. `.env.test` is gitignored; this file is not.
#
# The harness CREATES and DROPS databases on this server. It only ever touches
# names matching `app_harness_*_test`, and it refuses to run against a database
# that does not carry its own `_harness_schema` marker — but the server itself
# must still be one where a stray `DROP DATABASE` costs nothing.
#
# The database component of this URL is ignored: the harness connects to
# `postgres` for DDL and to `app_harness_<run>_w<n>_test` for the tests. It is
# the SERVER and the CREDENTIALS that this value supplies.
TEST_DATABASE_URL=postgres://postgres:password@localhost:5432/postgres

# Anything set here overrides `.env` for the test run only. Nothing else is
# required: `tests/helpers/run.ts` layers this file over the environment `.env`
# already provided, so only the values a test needs to differ belong here.
